Backport of upstream pygfx PR #1324 (open at the time of writing):
"Give bake functions the viewport size, not the canvas size"

    https://github.com/pygfx/pygfx/pull/1324

renderer.render(..., rect=...) already computes scene_lsize, the logical size
of the region being drawn into, but handed call_bake_functions the size of the
whole canvas.  The line shader's bake function uses that size to convert ndc to
logical pixels for the cumulative distance a dash pattern is measured along, so
a dashed line with thickness_space="screen" drawn into a sub-viewport came out
with its dashes scaled by the canvas/viewport ratio (measured: 12.0 px against
the 31.4 px the pattern asks for, on a 300 px viewport in a 900 px canvas).

The upstream commit also adds a test; it lives outside the sdist, so only the
pygfx/ hunk is backported here.

diff --git a/pygfx/renderers/wgpu/engine/renderer.py b/pygfx/renderers/wgpu/engine/renderer.py
index 3337dd7..1b993b2 100644
--- a/pygfx/renderers/wgpu/engine/renderer.py
+++ b/pygfx/renderers/wgpu/engine/renderer.py
@@ -742,7 +742,7 @@ class WgpuRenderer(RootEventHandler, Renderer):
         flat.collect_pipelines_container_groups(renderstate)
 
         # Enable pipelines to update data on the CPU.
-        flat.call_bake_functions(camera, logical_size)
+        flat.call_bake_functions(camera, scene_lsize)
 
         # Update *all* buffers and textures that have changed
         for resource in resource_update_registry.get_syncable_resources(flush=True):
